<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Mortgage Rate Trend Predictions</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif; }
  .header-nav { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .chart-container { position: relative; height: 350px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .expert-poll-box { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; border-radius: 5px; width: 350px; }
  .poll-option { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 8px 0; }
  .poll-option span:first-child { display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .poll-option .icon { margin-right: 10px; }
  .rate-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 20px; }
  .rate-table th, .rate-table td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 10px; text-align: left; }
  .rate-table th { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
  .quote-box { border-left: 5px solid #333; padding-left: 20px; margin: 40px 0; font-style: italic; }
  .author-card { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .author-card img { width: 80px; height: 80px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 20px; }
  .author-info h4 { margin: 0 0 5px 0; }
  .author-info p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9em; color: #555; }
  .list-item { margin-bottom: 10px; }
</style>

<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  div {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  h1, h2 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <div class="header-nav">
        <div><strong>Bankrate</strong></div>
        <div>
            <button style="padding: 8px 15px; background-color: #007bff; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer;">Create Account</button>
            <span style="margin-left: 15px; cursor: pointer;">&#x1F50D;</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
        <span style="color: #007bff; text-decoration: none;">MORTGAGES</span>
        <span style="float: right; font-size: 0.9em;"><a href="#" style="color: #007bff; text-decoration: none;">Advertiser Disclosure</a></span>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <h1>Expert Poll: Mortgage Rate Trend Predictions For Oct. 7-13, 2021</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <!-- Placeholder for the main chart image -->
        <div style="height: 100%; background-color: #e0e0e0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: #777;">
            [Visual representation of the rate trend chart]
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="flex-grow: 1;">
            <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;">Written by <span data-field="author.full_name">{{ author.full_name }}</span></div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;">Oct. 6, 2021 / 5 min read</div>
            <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
                <p>At Bankrate we strive to help you make smarter financial decisions. While we adhere to strict <a href="#" style="color: #007bff;">editorial integrity</a>, this post may contain references to products from our partners. Here's an explanation for <a href="#" style="color: #007bff;">how we make money</a>.</p>
                <p>Mortgage experts mostly expect rates to rise in the week ahead (Oct. 7-13). In response to Bankrate's weekly poll, 58 percent said rates will go up. Meanwhile, 33 percent said they would remain the same and just 8 percent expect them to fall. Calculate your monthly payment using Bankrate's <a href="#" style="color: #007bff;">mortgage calculator</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-left: 30px;">
            <div class="expert-poll-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Experts say rates will ...</h3>
                <div class="poll-option">
                    <span><span class="icon">&#9650;</span> Go up</span>
                    <span>{{ poll_results.go_up }}%</span>
                </div>
                <div class="poll-option">
                    <span><span class="icon">&#9644;</span> Stay the same</span>
                    <span>{{ poll_results.stay_same }}%</span>
                </div>
                <div class="poll-option">
                    <span><span class="icon">&#9660;</span> Go down</span>
                    <span>{{ poll_results.go_down }}%</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section">
        <h2>RATE TREND INDEX</h2>
        <h3>Experts predict where mortgage rates are headed</h3>
        <p>Week of Oct 7 - 13</p>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <!-- Placeholder for the pie chart image -->
        <div style="height: 300px; background-color: #e0e0e0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: #777;">
            [Visual representation of the pie chart]
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <div class="expert-poll-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Experts say rates will ...</h3>
            <div class="poll-option">
                <span><span class="icon">&#9650;</span> Go up</span>
                <span>{{ poll_results.go_up }}%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="poll-option">
                <span><span class="icon">&#9644;</span> Stay the same</span>
                <span>{{ poll_results.stay_same }}%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="poll-option">
                <span><span class="icon">&#9660;</span> Go down</span>
                <span>{{ poll_results.go_down }}%</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section" style="text-align: center;">
        <div class="quote-box">
            <p>"{{ quote.text }}"</p>
            <p>— <span data-field="quote.author_name">{{ quote.author_name }}</span>, <span data-field="quote.author_affiliation">{{ quote.author_affiliation }}</span></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px;">
            {% for expert in experts %}
            <div class="author-card" style="width: calc(33% - 20px);">
                <img src="#" alt="Expert Photo">
                <div class="author-info">
                    <h4><span data-field="expert.full_name">{{ expert.full_name }}</span></h4>
                    <p><span data-field="expert.title">{{ expert.title }}</span>, <span data-field="expert.affiliation">{{ expert.affiliation }}</span></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Long-term mortgage rates will increase in the coming week. 10-year Treasury Note yields continue to rise as a result of sobering economic news – lowering growth expectations, debt limit brinksmanship between the Republicans and Democrats, questions about the supply chains of almost everything and inflation. China's issues with real estate, etc. The increase in the 10-year Treasury yields will result in upward pressure on mortgage rates. Long-term mortgage rates will increase in the coming week.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Rates may edge up slightly this week but it's getting a bit more complicated as the stock market and Treasury markets are anything but steady! It would appear the expectation is for rates to start moving higher but with so many potential landmines ahead anything is possible!</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Mortgage rates go up. Here's a parody based on Gwen Stefani's 2006 hit, "The Sweet Escape." "Bears can make it better. And tell Oil bulls, now wouldn't that</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section">
        <p>be sweet? (Sweet escape, sweet escape)." Unfortunately, mortgage rates are rising due to uncertainty over the U.S. budget, debt, supply chains, and rising energy costs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px;">
            {% for expert in experts %}
            <div class="author-card" style="width: calc(33% - 20px);">
                <img src="#" alt="Expert Photo">
                <div class="author-info">
                    <h4><span data-field="expert.full_name">{{ expert.full_name }}</span></h4>
                    <p><span data-field="expert.title">{{ expert.title }}</span>, <span data-field="expert.affiliation">{{ expert.affiliation }}</span></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section" style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
            <h3 style="margin: 0;">8% say rates will go down <span style="font-size: 0.7em;">&#9660;</span></h3>
            <div style="width: 30%;">
                <p>Robert Brusca</p>
                <p><span data-field="expert.title">{{ expert.title }}</span>, <span data-field="expert.affiliation">{{ expert.affiliation }}</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section" style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
            <h3 style="margin: 0;">33% say unchanged <span style="font-size: 0.7em;">—</span></h3>
            <div style="width: 30%;">
                <p>Dick Lepre</p>
                <p><span data-field="expert.title">{{ expert.title }}</span>, <span data-field="expert.affiliation">{{ expert.affiliation }}</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Trend: Flat. Confusion reigns. Pandemic-induced supply disruptions are causing inflation. This should increase mortgage rates. On the other hand, massive fiscal deficits will likely restrain GDP, which should keep rates low. We are in a situation we have never been before.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Unchanged for this week. With the 10-year trading at 1.51 percent we are almost exactly where we were last week (1.52 percent). ADP reported better than expected numbers in the private sector but the non-farm payrolls are what the market is waiting for on Friday and it is expected that unemployment will come down 0.1 percent. We are clearly more jobs to fill, we have all seen help wanted signs everywhere so it is a bit of a conundrum as to why unemployment is not lower. Lastly, we have inflation, a global energy crunch and the Fed tapering lingering behind the curtain.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <p>Unchanged. Jobs Friday is coming up, so that will be the event that can move bond yields. The ADP report came in as a nice beat, but for now, Friday will be the only big event this week. The 10-year yield did have a slide-down of almost 10 basis points this past week but is currently at 1.51 percent. We might be range-bound with bond yields until we can get a clear break; remember to focus on the close of Friday on the 10-year yield, not the intraday action.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section">
        <p>About the Bankrate.com Rate Trend Index</p>
        <p>Bankrate's panel of experts is comprised of economists, mortgage bankers, mortgage brokers and other industry experts who provide residential first mortgages to consumers. Results from Bankrate.com's Mortgage Rate Trend Index are released each Thursday.com</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">
        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 10px;">Stay on top of ever-changing rates</h3>
        <p>Get customized rate alerts delivered directly to your inbox.</p>
        <form style="max-width: 400px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <input type="email" placeholder="Email" style="width: 100%; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid #ccc;">
            <button type="submit" style="padding: 10px 20px; background-color: #007bff; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer;">Subscribe</button>
        </form>
        <p style="font-size: 0.8em; margin-top: 15px;">By clicking 'Subscribe', I agree to Bankrate.com's <a href="#" style="color: #007bff;">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="#" style="color: #007bff;">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="content-section" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">
        <h2>ABOUT THE AUTHOR</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <div class="author-card">
            <img src="#" alt="Author Photo">
            <div class="author-info">
                <h4><span data-field="author.full_name">{{ author.full_name }}</span></h4>
                <p><span data-field="author.bio">{{ author.bio }}</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <h3>Highlights</h3>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="author.highlight_1">{{ author.highlight_1 }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="author.highlight_2">{{ author.highlight_2 }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <h3>Experience</h3>
        <p><span data-field="author.experience">{{ author.experience }}</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
        <h3>In the media</h3>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="author.media_1">{{ author.media_1 }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="author.media_2">{{ author.media_2 }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>


